Source: hyperv
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: hyperv-for-linux maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/olljanat-ai/hyperv-for-linux

Package: hyperv
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, systemd, curl, ca-certificates, libarchive-tools
Recommends: linux-image-hyperv
Description: Microsoft Hypervisor for Linux (installer meta-package)
 Downloads the Microsoft Hypervisor loader and firmware blobs from
 packages.microsoft.com/azurelinux/3.0/prod/ at install time and
 registers a systemd-boot entry that chainloads HvLoader.efi from the
 ESP.
 .
 The Microsoft binaries are NOT redistributed by this package; the
 postinst fetches them on the target machine, where the user accepts
 Microsoft's license at install time.
